&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46079073"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HN Discussion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href='https://gwern.net/doc/psychology/linguistics/2024-fedorenko.pdf'&gt;Read Original Article&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top 3 Comments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;andai:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;When I was a kid a friend asked me, &amp;quot;Hey, you speak three languages. Which one do you think in?&amp;quot;&lt;p&gt;I was bemused, and thought... &amp;quot;people think in words?&amp;quot;&lt;p&gt;Apparently people with ADHD or Autism can develop the inner voice later in life.&lt;p&gt;In my 20s, language colonized my brain. Took me years of meditation to get some peace and quiet back...&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;krackers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Doesn&amp;#x27;t hellen keller provide a counterexample? She seemed to imply pretty strongly that before acquisition of language she operated more on stimulus and bodily perception rather than higher-level thought.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;netfortius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Excellent, comprehensive, extremely thorough work behind all this. Maturana would love it!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
